INSERT INTO `wp_8_posts` VALUES (1,1,'2015-12-07 07:53:42','2015-12-07 07:53:42','PACT - Peoples Alliance for Children and Teachers is an initiative by YieldMore.org begun in September 2017 that is a platform for discussion, debate and action in the field of Education.\r\n\r\nPACT is a coming together of all these involved in the holistic development of the child. First described by <a href=\"https://twitter.com/LearnYMO\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Rani</a> <a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/about/?node=pact\">here</a>, PACT is a series of digests for parents, administrators, children and teachers, the influencers and the influenced who help shape and build a better tomorrow.\r\n\r\nThis is an invitation to one and all to give ideas on topics that should be covered, who can make videos, whether to setup an interactive Q&A site, who else to involve, what existing platforms and resources are available, a helper directory, some information for consideration by parents and teachers and what activities the children can do. These could include social awareness, ways to combat stress and peer pressure, developing ones sense of value and identity, inspiring ideas, tools and devices, holistic education etc.','What is PACT','','publish','closed','open','','about','','','2018-01-20 08:15:51','2018-01-20 02:45:51','',0,'http://stats.yieldmore.org/?page_id=2',1,'page','',0),(3,1,'2015-12-07 07:53:44','2015-12-07 07:53:44','General chit-chat','General','','publish','closed','closed','','general','','','2015-12-07 07:53:44','2015-12-07 07:53:44','',0,'http://stats.yieldmore.org/ask/forums/general/',0,'forum','',0),(4,1,'2015-12-07 07:53:44','2015-12-07 07:53:44','I am the first topic in your new forums.','Hello World!','','publish','closed','closed','','hello-world','','','2015-12-07 07:53:44','2015-12-07 07:53:44','',3,'http://stats.yieldmore.org/ask/topic/hello-world/',0,'topic','',0),(5,1,'2015-12-07 07:53:44','2015-12-07 07:53:44','Oh, and this is what a reply looks like.','Re: Hello World!','','publish','closed','closed','','re-hello-world','','','2015-12-09 13:43:46','2015-12-09 08:13:46','',4,'http://stats.yieldmore.org/ask/reply/re-hello-world/',1,'reply','',0),(14,1,'2018-01-19 10:18:11','2018-01-19 04:48:11','[info]\r\nlink: http://gg1952.blogspot.in/2017/12/inside-black-box-revisted-again.html\r\nsource: https://www.rdc.udel.edu/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/InsideBlackBox.pdf\r\n[/info]\r\n\r\n','Inside the Black Box','','publish','open','open','','inside-the-black-box','','','2018-01-19 10:18:11','2018-01-19 04:48:11','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=14',0,'post','',0),(15,1,'2018-01-20 08:14:49','2018-01-20 02:44:49','PACT - Peoples Alliance for Children and Teachers is an initiative by YieldMore.org begun in September 2017 that is a platform for discussion, debate and action in the field of Education.\n\nPACT is a coming together of all these involved in the holistic development of the child. First described by Rani <a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/about/?node=pact\">here</a>, PACT is a series of digests for parents, administrators, children and teachers, the influencers and the influenced who help shape and build a better tomorrow.','What is PACT','','inherit','closed','closed','','1-autosave-v1','','','2018-01-20 08:14:49','2018-01-20 02:44:49','',1,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/1-autosave-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(16,1,'2018-01-20 08:31:52','2018-01-20 03:01:52','{{unknown}}','','','publish','closed','closed','','659cbf27dca9e11187bbf410fc1b258a','','','2018-01-20 08:31:52','2018-01-20 03:01:52','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/659cbf27dca9e11187bbf410fc1b258a/',0,'oembed_cache','',0),(17,1,'2018-01-21 11:22:02','2018-01-21 05:52:02','You may visit the following links (this page - <a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/pl\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">http://yieldmore.org/pl)</a>:\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/ie\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">http://yieldmore.org/ie</a> - Instrumental Enrichment - a metacognitive program for developing ones ability to better meet goals by improving the process of input-elaboration-output.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/wve\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/wve</a> - WorldView Explorations - A trademarked set of 22 lessons for school and college children developed by the Institute of Noetic Sciences, founded in 1973.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/school\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/school</a> - a curated list of 150 English songs for children, for better appreciation of music and culture. -\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/values\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/values</a> - A series of classroom exercises developed by Prof Naidu.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/pw\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/pw</a> - Peaceworks - Our program for guiding, counselling and skill development.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/tct\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/tct</a> - The Compass Team - with India\'s first copyrighted, holistic child development program.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/pactg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">/pactg</a> - The PACT discussion Google Group.\r\n\r\nNB: these are short urls and do not end with a / [slash].','PACT Links','','publish','closed','closed','','links','','','2018-01-21 11:29:43','2018-01-21 05:59:43','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?page_id=17',0,'page','',0),(18,1,'2018-01-21 11:10:14','2018-01-21 05:40:14','Instrumental Enrichment (IE) a metacognitive program for developing ones ability to better meet goals by improving the process of input-elaboration-output. It was developed by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuven_Feuerstein\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prof. Reuven Feuerstein</a>, a clinical, developmental and cognitive psychologist [<a href=\"http://www.icelp.info/about/professor-reuven-feuerstein.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">icelp.info</a>]\r\n\r\nTo know more about doing the program / becoming a facilitator, please contact Rani - 9942912041.\r\n\r\n<!--more-->\r\nSee our original post from July 2015 here:\r\n\r\nhttp://yieldmore.org/programs/instrumental-enrichment/','Instrumental Enrichment','','publish','open','open','','instrumental-enrichment','','','2018-01-21 14:01:52','2018-01-21 08:31:52','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=18',0,'post','',0),(19,1,'2018-01-21 13:40:36','2018-01-21 08:10:36','This is a Google Groups Forum which is embedded below. You need to be signed in to Google to see it.\r\n<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/pactg\" target=\"_blank\">http://yieldmore.org/pactg</a>\r\n\r\n<!--more-->\r\n<iframe id=\"forum_embed\"\r\n  src=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/embed/?place=forum/pact-ym&showsearch=true&showpopout=true&showtabs=true&parenturl=http%3A%2F%2Fyieldmore.org%2Fpact%2F\"\r\n  scrolling=\"no\"\r\n  frameborder=\"0\"\r\n  width=\"100%\"\r\n  height=\"600\">\r\n</iframe>\r\n','PACT Forum','','publish','closed','closed','','forum','','','2018-01-21 13:58:32','2018-01-21 08:28:32','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?page_id=19',0,'page','',0),(21,1,'2018-01-21 14:01:45','2018-01-21 08:31:45','Instrumental Enrichment (IE) a metacognitive program for developing ones ability to better meet goals by improving the process of input-elaboration-output. It was developed by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuven_Feuerstein\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prof. Reuven Feuerstein</a>, a clinical, developmental and cognitive psychologist [<a href=\"http://www.icelp.info/about/professor-reuven-feuerstein.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">icelp.info</a>]\n\nTo know more about doing the program / becoming a facilitator, please contact Rani - 9942912041.\n\n\nSee our original post from July 2015 here:\n\nhttp://yieldmore.org/programs/instrumental-enrichment/','Instrumental Enrichment','','inherit','closed','closed','','18-autosave-v1','','','2018-01-21 14:01:45','2018-01-21 08:31:45','',18,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/18-autosave-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(20,1,'2018-02-03 04:56:10','2018-02-02 23:26:10','This is a Google Groups Forum which is embedded below. You need to be signed in to Google to see it.\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/journalofsocialwork\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/journalofsocialwork</a>\n\n<!--more-->\n<iframe id=\"forum_embed\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/embed/?place=forum/pact-ym&amp;showsearch=true&amp;showpopout=true&amp;showtabs=true&amp;parenturl=http%3A%2F%2Fyieldmore.org%2Fpact%2F\" width=\"100%\" height=\"600\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\">\n</iframe>','PACT Forum','','inherit','closed','closed','','19-autosave-v1','','','2018-02-03 04:56:10','2018-02-02 23:26:10','',19,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/19-autosave-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(23,1,'2018-02-08 23:32:58','2018-02-08 18:02:58','<iframe width=\"525\" height=\"394\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/videoseries?list=PLNEB1ItETG4VfoReWTEjm3odumCOgXa2l\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; encrypted-media\" allowfullscreen></iframe>','','','publish','closed','closed','','a34c94f59231f1c6c584c95c45cfc89f','','','2018-02-08 23:32:58','2018-02-08 18:02:58','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/a34c94f59231f1c6c584c95c45cfc89f/',0,'oembed_cache','',0),(24,1,'2018-02-08 23:32:59','2018-02-08 18:02:59','<iframe width=\"214\" height=\"161\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/videoseries?list=PLNEB1ItETG4VfoReWTEjm3odumCOgXa2l\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; encrypted-media\" allowfullscreen></iframe>','','','publish','closed','closed','','b87956b8db933583195903dd707bdc79','','','2018-02-08 23:32:59','2018-02-08 18:02:59','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/b87956b8db933583195903dd707bdc79/',0,'oembed_cache','',0),(31,1,'2018-04-24 19:06:49','2018-04-24 13:36:49','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p1RY1BpIaSE\r\n\r\n[info]\r\nsource: http://brianraymondking.com/2017/11/06/episode-10-overcoming-your-fear-of-an-ld-diagnosis-an-interview-with-benjamin-bodnar/\r\n[/info]\r\n\r\nTo truly champion the strengths that will allow you to succeed while living with an LD diagnosis, you must first free yourself of all resistance to the diagnosis. \r\n\r\nFacing the diagnosis of a learning disability such as dyslexia, ADHD, autism, and many other conditions, can be one of the most harrowing events of parenthood. Parents who must endure this difficult revelation must, therefore, be treated with the utmost compassion and patience as they process the information and begin to plan for the lifelong ramifications of their childâ€™s condition. However, even parents who have the full support and empathy of their immediate families, as well as the guidance of the social and educational communities, sometimes struggle to cope effectively with their childâ€™s reality and engage in recalcitrant behavior with respect to the diagnosis.\r\n\r\nThis parental resistance can emanate from multiple sources, but the principal influences causing parentsâ€™ discomfort with active management and intervention are:\r\n\r\n1) fear of social isolation of both the LD individual,\r\n\r\n2) fear of stigmatization of the LD individualâ€™s family in their social and professional communities,\r\n\r\n3) pride in the parentsâ€™ own academic achievements and abilities and resulting disbelief in the birth of a child unlikely to replicate those feats,\r\n\r\n4) financial implications of addressing a learning disability, and\r\n\r\n5) unwillingness to devote the additional time required to cooperate with the external sources of support. In these unfortunate scenarios, the learning disabled child or young adult is greatly imperiled as he or she is endangered of progressing through education and life without the single most crucial support structure necessary to develop into a functional adult.\r\n\r\nLearning disabled individuals who do not have the backing of their own homes are very unlikely to compensate even with expert support from his or her social and school environments, rendering these other secondary support structures largely ineffectual.\r\n\r\nIt is therefore of great importance that learning disabled individuals and the community of stakeholders around them develop methods and protocols to engage recalcitrant parents in addressing special educational needs in non-stigmatizing ways that reassure the parents that LD management techniques are trustworthy and beneficial to the child or young adultâ€™s long-term prosperity.\r\n\r\nTopics we cover in this episode include: \r\n\r\n1) How LD individuals, especially those of adult or near adult age, can be effective self-advocates in the face of denial, gaslighting, and invalidation relating to the diagnosis and its implications, and how we can instill a sense of pride in these individuals,\r\n\r\n2) How recalcitrant parents can be taught the numerous upsides not only of effective intervention but of the disability itself, namely, that attending their childâ€™s learning differences are highly useful attributes in school and business (which are also highly regarded in the social circles that may be the chief factor fueling their resistance to acknowledgement) and that the differences are things of which the parents themselves can be proud,\r\n\r\n3) How we can impress upon parents the benefits of proper management, up to and including financial and social benefits resulting from greater prospects for the child with intervention as proactive as possible, and\r\n\r\n4) How we need a compassionate but firm approach that teaches parents and other caregivers that being true to oneself and to their loved one with an LD is a path to prosperity while playing a contrived role is one destined for frustration for both them and the LD individual.','Overcoming your fear of an LD (Learning Disability) diagnosis','','publish','open','open','','overcoming-your-fear-of-a-learning-disability-diagnosis','','','2018-04-24 19:06:49','2018-04-24 13:36:49','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=31',0,'post','',0),(29,24,'2018-03-25 20:18:24','0000-00-00 00:00:00','','Education','','draft','open','open','','','','','2018-03-25 20:18:24','2018-03-25 14:48:24','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=29',0,'post','',0),(30,1,'2018-03-28 14:40:04','2018-03-28 09:10:04','A question on \"What did you really learn in school\" was posed by the people of <a href=\"http://ankuram-mandir.org\" target=\"_blank\">Ankuram</a> and these were the replies.\r\n\r\n<h3>Prem</h3>\r\n<iframe src=\"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fpremkumar1803%2Fvideos%2F10155212616851175%2F&show_text=0&width=560\" width=\"560\" height=\"314\" style=\"border:none;overflow:hidden\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"0\" allowTransparency=\"true\" allowFullScreen=\"true\"></iframe>\r\n\r\n<h3>Saakshi</h3>\r\n<iframe src=\"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fsaakshi666%2Fvideos%2F10160231290995201%2F&show_text=0&width=261\" width=\"261\" height=\"476\" style=\"border:none;overflow:hidden\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"0\" allowTransparency=\"true\" allowFullScreen=\"true\"></iframe>\r\n\r\n<h3>Imran</h3>\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NRMAz6HPvMw\r\n','What did you really learn in school','','publish','open','open','','what-did-you-really-learn-in-school','','','2018-03-28 14:40:55','2018-03-28 09:10:55','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=30',0,'post','',0),(33,1,'2018-06-03 15:02:47','2018-06-03 09:32:47','[info]\r\nsource: https://www.cde.ca.gov/sp/cd/re/caqdevelopment.asp\r\nsource: https://www.scholastic.com/teachers/articles/teaching-content/ages-stages-bonding-attachment/\r\n[/info]\r\n\r\nChoosing quality care that is in a healthy and safe environment should be your number one priority. Look for child care that stimulates and encourages your childâ€™s physical, intellectual, and social growth. Keep your childâ€™s age and personality in mind when looking for the program that best meets his needs. Understanding what makes your child feel secure and knowing the activities he enjoys and will learn from will make a difference in your final child care decision.\r\n\r\nPersonality\r\nEach child has his own personality and responds to caregivers or experiences differently. Just like adults, children may have outgoing, shy, or even-tempered natures. Your caregiver should be in tune with your childâ€™s special personality and treat your child in a positive and caring manner that agrees with his special personality. This is crucial to nurturing his healthy emotional growth.  By understanding your childâ€™s personality, you and your caregiver can help him succeed by offering care, activities, and discipline that best fit his needs.\r\n\r\nDevelopmental stages\r\nAs your child grows, you may find yourself searching for clues to her behavior. As a parent, you may hear the words â€œdevelopmental stages.â€ This is just another way of saying your child is moving through a certain time period in the growing-up process. At times, she may be fascinated with her hands, her feet, and her mouth. As she grows, she may get into everything. Lock your doors and cabinets, and take a deep breath during those exploration years! Then there will be an age when independence is all she wants. At every stage, what she needs is your love, understanding, and time.\r\n\r\nParent Tip\r\nRecent brain research indicates that birth to age three are the most important years in a childâ€™s development. Here are some tips to consider during your childâ€™s early years:\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Be warm, loving, and responsive.</li>\r\n	<li>Talk, read, and sing to your child.</li>\r\n	<li>Establish routines and rituals.</li>\r\n	<li>Encourage safe explorations and play.</li>\r\n	<li>Make TV watching selective.</li>\r\n	<li>Use discipline as an opportunity to teach.</li>\r\n	<li>Recognize that each child is unique.</li>\r\n	<li>Choose quality child care and stay involved.</li>\r\n	<li>Take care of yourself.</li>\r\n</ul>','Stages of Child Development','','publish','open','open','','stages-of-child-development','','','2018-06-03 15:02:47','2018-06-03 09:32:47','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=33',0,'post','',0),(34,1,'2018-06-15 22:01:41','2018-06-15 16:31:41','To Youngsters as they set out to win their dreams... Co-concombatant on this wonderful journey of life - what will YOUR VERSE BE? Write in to have your take at inspiring youth posted here.\r\n\r\nhttp://yieldmore.org/express/imran/keep-smiling/\r\n\r\n<blockquote>We don\'t read and write poetry because it\'s cute. We read and write poetry because we are members of the human race. And the human race is filled with passion. And medicine, law, business, engineering, these are noble pursuits and necessary to sustain life. But poetry, beauty, romance, love, these are what we stay alive for. To quote from Whitman, \"O me! O life!... of the questions of these recurring; of the endless trains of the faithless... of cities filled with the foolish; what good amid these, O me, O life?\" Answer. That you are here - that life exists, and identity; that the powerful play goes on and you may contribute a verse. That the powerful play *goes on* and you may contribute a verse. <a href=\"http://www.rjgeib.com/thoughts/dp-society/dp-society.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">What will your verse be</a>? - <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0097165/quotes\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Dead Poet\'s Society</a></blockquote>\r\n\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aS1esgRV4Rc&list=PLsuI89eMBnMHeQvgPaHV23_t3xIUmbkKm','Inspiring Youth','','publish','open','open','','inspiring-youth','','\nhttp://yieldmore.org/express/imran/keep-smiling/','2018-06-19 23:29:29','2018-06-19 17:59:29','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=34',0,'post','',0),(35,1,'2018-06-19 23:28:12','2018-06-19 17:58:12','To Youngsters as they set out to win their dreams... Co-concombatant on this wonderful journey of life - what will YOUR VERSE BE? Write in to have your take at inspiring youth posted here.\n\nhttp://yieldmore.org/express/imran/keep-smiling/\n\n<blockquote>We don\'t read and write poetry because it\'s cute. We read and write poetry because we are members of the human race. And the human race is filled with passion. And medicine, law, business, engineering, these are noble pursuits and necessary to sustain life. But poetry, beauty, romance, love, these are what we stay alive for. To quote from Whitman, \"O me! O life!... of the questions of these recurring; of the endless trains of the faithless... of cities filled with the foolish; what good amid these, O me, O life?\" Answer. That you are here - that life exists, and identity; that the powerful play goes on and you may contribute a verse. That the powerful play *goes on* and you may contribute a verse. <a href=\"http://www.rjgeib.com/thoughts/dp-society/dp-society.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">What will your verse be</a>? - <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0097165/quotes\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Dead Poet\'s Society</a></blockquote>\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aS1esgRV4Rc&list=PLsuI89eMBnMHeQvgPaHV23_t3xIUmbkKm','Inspiring Youth','','inherit','closed','closed','','34-autosave-v1','','','2018-06-19 23:28:12','2018-06-19 17:58:12','',34,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/uncategorised/34-autosave-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(40,1,'2018-08-30 16:30:53','2018-08-30 11:00:53','[ads id=hst]\r\n\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqOPwGModbE\r\n\r\nWe <a href=\"http://headstreamtech.in\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Headstream Technologies</a>, founded in 2013 are here to facilitate excellence in the field of teaching and administration. Most educational institutions are begun with a vision of preparing young minds with diverse skills and in developing their many talents. We are here to help you translate that vision down to all levels of your teaching (and non-teaching) staff with our â€œEducator Effectivenessâ€ platform <a href=\"https://www.edlusion.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">EDLUSION</a>.\r\n\r\nWhy choose us?\r\n\r\nTeachers are shown at year beginning just what their growth-path is, how they will be evaluated at each stage of your evaluation cycle, plan to take / be given courses that keep their skills and techniques up-to date, map out how their personal goals align to institutional ones etc. We bring the best of Evaluation and Course Management jointly in this one offering with our in-depth knowledge of current trends and teacher Professional Development and Mentoring process.','Edlusion','','publish','open','open','','edlusion','','','2018-08-30 16:34:14','2018-08-30 11:04:14','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=40',0,'post','',0),(39,31,'2018-06-21 18:29:12','2018-06-21 12:59:12','Hi,\r\n\r\nI\'m Shruti Jayasimha, a special educator by profession. I enjoy teaching children.','Milestones Learning Centre','','publish','open','open','','mlc','','','2018-06-21 18:29:12','2018-06-21 12:59:12','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=39',0,'post','',0),(41,1,'2018-09-07 20:38:04','2018-09-07 15:08:04','A collection of articles, begun on Teachers day 2018 - Sep 5th from our supporters on the topic of teaching.\r\n\r\n[work config fol=interactive/td2018][/work]','Teachers Day 2018','','publish','open','open','','teachers-day-2018','','','2018-09-07 20:38:04','2018-09-07 15:08:04','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=41',0,'post','',0),(42,1,'2019-05-17 19:43:09','2019-05-17 14:13:09','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An educator for the past 21 years, <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Vidya Shankar (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"http://cascadefls.org/people/vidya-shankar/\" target=\"_blank\">Vidya Shankar</a> founded <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"CASCADE Family Learning Center (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"http://cascadefls.org/about-cascade/\" target=\"_blank\">CASCADE Family Learning Center</a> that focuses more on the first 3 [critical] years of child development.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This illustrated story called \"<a href=\"http://yieldmore.org/media/books/education/idac-danger-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Danger School (opens in a new tab)\">Danger School</a>\" better sets the context from which her style / approach to Family Learning is derived.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Vidya Shankar','','publish','open','open','','vidya-shankar','','','2019-05-17 19:43:09','2019-05-17 14:13:09','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=42',0,'post','',0),(43,1,'2019-06-08 09:33:46','2019-06-08 04:03:46','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>From: <a href=\"https://my995fm.iheart.com/content/2019-06-07-katy-perry-reveals-why-she-wants-a-long-engagement/\">https://my995fm.iheart.com/content/2019-06-07-katy-perry-reveals-why-she-wants-a-long-engagement/</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For parents to remind friends and their teenagers...</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Orlando Bloom&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://onairwithryan.iheart.com/content/2019-02-15-katy-perry-orlando-bloom-are-engaged-see-her-ring/\">proposed to Katy Perry in the grandest of ways&nbsp;</a></strong>on Valentine\'s Day, but don\'t expect the couple to be walking down the aisle any time soon. During a brief chat with UK\'s&nbsp;<em><strong><a href=\"https://planetradio.co.uk/podcasts/kiss-breakfast-wrap/listen/17050/\">Kiss Breakfast Wrap</a></strong></em>, the \"Never Really Over\" singer was asked if she was planning her big day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>â€œWell yeah, one step at a time,\" she said. \"Definitely, you know, trying to, like, lay the good emotional foundation for the lifetime of commitment, which is, like, a big deal, you know?â€<br>\n</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The 34-year-old was briefly married to&nbsp;<strong>Russell Brand</strong>between 2010 and 2012, so she has every reason to take this engagement slowly and make sure she and her partner are the best they can be for each other before saying \"I do.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Take Relationships Slowly','','publish','open','open','','take-relationships-slowly','','','2019-06-08 09:34:54','2019-06-08 04:04:54','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=43',0,'post','',0),(46,1,'2019-08-27 03:06:39','2019-08-26 21:36:39','<!-- wp:core-embed/instagram {\"url\":\"https://www.instagram.com/tv/B1jxx6cAUOV/?igshid=gccqiu4rpqzy\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"instagram\",\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed-instagram wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.instagram.com/tv/B1jxx6cAUOV/?igshid=gccqiu4rpqzy\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:core-embed/instagram -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Life is a battlefield boys and girls, and the casualties could be your hearts and souls...</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So choose carefully what your studying or telling your children to study. I\'m an Electrical Engineer turned programmer and I\'m lucky that I love both, but now I wonder if a GAP YEAR would have done me better... Or and entrepreneurial incubator early in my career!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','To Doctor or Not to Doctor','','publish','open','open','','to-doctor-or-not-to-doctor','','','2019-08-27 03:06:39','2019-08-26 21:36:39','',0,'http://yieldmore.org/pact/?p=46',0,'post','',0);
